# Next.js Upgrade

- Always run the official Next.js codemod first.
- Do not do large refactors during an upgrade — only changes required for compatibility.
- After each significant step, run:
  1. `npm run build` (or npx)
  2. `npm run format-and-fix` (or npx)
  3. `npm run test` (or npx) (if available)
- When working with the App Router:
  - Always `await` `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()`, `headers()`, and `draftMode()`
  - Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only when truly needed
- Do not remove old code until the new version passes all checks.
- At the end of the migration, verify:
  - The app starts (`npm run dev` (or npx))
  - No errors in the browser console
  - The database connection works
